[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hello everyone! I have successfully formalised Hochster's Theorem: every spectral topological space is homeomorphic to the prime spectrum of a commutative ring. Here is the link to my repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/FMLJohn/Hochster\">https://github.com/FMLJohn/Hochster</a>.</p>\n<p>The theorem has been stated as the following, which can be found in Hochster/Section7.lean:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exists_nonempty_homeomorph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SpectralSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrimeSpectrum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 574354332,
        "sender_full_name": "Fangming Li (John)",
        "timestamp": 1771351191
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Congratulations! You might be the first human I've met who has read the proof :-)</p>",
        "id": 574394799,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1771366230
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was curious about this and just tried the github link, but it doesn't seem to work for me. Is the repository still public?</p>",
        "id": 609117529,
        "sender_full_name": "Robert Shlyakhtenko",
        "timestamp": 1783560283
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We made the repo private but only because we wanted to do experiments with getting AI to formalise the same theorem, it will certainly be made public again in the future</p>",
        "id": 609146791,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1783578161
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In the past few days, I have made some further progress. I have managed to formalise the extension of Hochster's Theorem to morphisms: every spectral map between spectral topological spaces is essentially the comap of a ring homomorphism. This result has been stated as the following, which can also be found in Hochster/Section7.lean in the same repository:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSpectralMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">exist_comap_comp_homeomorph_eq_comp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SpectralSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SpectralSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSpectralMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→+*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrimeSpectrum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrimeSpectrum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">PrimeSpectrum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Due to the AI experiment, the code is not publicly available now. It will be made publicly available in the future.</p>",
        "id": 609494048,
        "sender_full_name": "Fangming Li (John)",
        "timestamp": 1783700101
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Nice! Does the choice of S and T depend on f?</p>",
        "id": 609501331,
        "sender_full_name": "Andrew Yang",
        "timestamp": 1783702410
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No. As long as <code>X</code> and <code>Y</code> do not change, the choice of <code>S</code> and <code>T</code> remains unchanged.</p>",
        "id": 609504605,
        "sender_full_name": "Fangming Li (John)",
        "timestamp": 1783703447
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"566592\">Fangming Li (John)</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/116395-maths/topic/Formalising.20Hochster.27s.20Theorem/near/609504605\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>No. As long as <code>X</code> and <code>Y</code> do not change, the choice of <code>S</code> and <code>T</code> remains unchanged.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>So maybe you want to rephrase your conclusion as <code>∃ (S T : Type u) (_ : CommRing S) (_ : CommRing T), (f : X → Y) → IsSpectralMap f → ∃ (h : S →+* T) (h₁ : X ≃ₜ PrimeSpectrum T) (h₂ : Y ≃ₜ PrimeSpectrum S), PrimeSpectrum.comap h ∘ h₁ = h₂ ∘ f</code></p>",
        "id": 609520424,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1783708168
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you so much! I have changed the statement into the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exist_forall_exists_comap_comp_homeomorph_eq_comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SpectralSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SpectralSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrimeSpectrum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrimeSpectrum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSpectralMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→+*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">PrimeSpectrum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 609537459,
        "sender_full_name": "Fangming Li (John)",
        "timestamp": 1783714930
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does S and T depend on both X and Y? If S depends only on Y and T only on X, does h₁ and h₂ depend on both X and Y? <a href=\"https://mathoverflow.net/questions/508583/seeking-a-nice-or-simple-functorial-construction-of-a-commutative-ring-from#comment1325062_508583\">A comment</a> by Benjamin Steinberg on MO indicates that Chapter 7 of Hochster shows that there is no functor from spectral spaces to commutative rings that is a right inverse to Spec, so things must break at some point, but maybe you can still define Hom(X,Y)→Hom(R(Y),R(X))=Hom(S,T) and they just don't respect composition.</p>\n<p>Update: on reading the <a href=\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/1995344\">paper</a>, one of the rings depend on both spaces:<br>\n<img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"961x577\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/OT02J4MUWzXroxbd38f7ufxZ/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/OT02J4MUWzXroxbd38f7ufxZ/image.png/840x560.webp\"></p>",
        "id": 609550413,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1783721637
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes. Each of <code>T</code> and <code>h₁</code> depends on both <code>X</code> and <code>Y</code>. Both <code>S</code> and <code>h₂</code> only depend on <code>Y</code>.</p>",
        "id": 609553814,
        "sender_full_name": "Fangming Li (John)",
        "timestamp": 1783724343
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"566592\">Fangming Li (John)</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/116395-maths/topic/Formalising.20Hochster.27s.20Theorem/near/609553814\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yes. Each of <code>T</code> and <code>h₁</code> depends on both <code>X</code> and <code>Y</code>. Both <code>S</code> and <code>h₂</code> only depend on <code>Y</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Is it possible to rephrase a universe polymorphic version? Is this correct?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exist_forall_exists_comap_comp_homeomorph_eq_comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SpectralSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrimeSpectrum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SpectralSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">],</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrimeSpectrum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 609611445,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1783779771
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think when using this universe polymorphic version, Lean has some trouble to determine what the universe v is.</p>",
        "id": 609611574,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1783779900
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes! A polymorphic version exists. I have just formalised the following statement:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exist_forall_exist_forall_exists_comap_comp_homeomorph_eq_comp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SpectralSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrimeSpectrum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><